WEBVTT

00:11.010 --> 00:13.013
[gloomy music]

00:39.956 --> 00:41.124
That woman…

00:42.542 --> 00:43.835
I killed her.

00:46.796 --> 00:47.797
[sighs]

00:49.174 --> 00:51.426
Everyone was forced to play the game.

00:52.886 --> 00:54.095
It wasn't your fault.

00:57.974 --> 00:59.517
What the hell is all this?

01:02.896 --> 01:04.814
Who knows? I know I don't.

01:05.690 --> 01:06.608
But…

01:08.526 --> 01:11.196
It amazes me
that I'm willing to do anything

01:12.280 --> 01:13.615
just so that I can survive.

01:17.410 --> 01:19.954
[Usagi] If we didn't want to do that,
we might as well just die.

02:11.548 --> 02:13.550
[suspenseful music]

02:22.100 --> 02:24.269
[music intensifying]

02:29.357 --> 02:31.359
[theme music]

03:32.462 --> 03:34.505
[birds chirping]

03:42.680 --> 03:44.432
My visa ends today.

03:46.893 --> 03:47.769
[sighs]

03:49.187 --> 03:50.438
[marker clicks]

03:53.733 --> 03:56.861
[Shibuki] I worked so hard.
Did everything to get into that company.

03:59.322 --> 04:01.282
I even hooked up with someone I hated.

04:01.824 --> 04:03.243
[exhales deeply]

04:04.035 --> 04:06.079
And I finally got the promotion.

04:07.288 --> 04:08.581
[Shibuki moans]

04:08.665 --> 04:09.958
Saori…

04:10.041 --> 04:11.834
I talked to the HR department.

04:12.752 --> 04:17.757
[woman] Cypher Bank Holdings
strongly recommends Saori Shibuki

04:17.840 --> 04:21.261
as the new team leader of AI development.

04:21.344 --> 04:24.472
SPECIAL PROMOTION FOR ASSISTANT
IN THE DEVELOPMENT TEAM

04:26.391 --> 04:27.934
I'll survive this game

04:28.893 --> 04:30.770
and return to my original life.

04:32.939 --> 04:35.275
[Chota] Arisu! Karube!

04:35.775 --> 04:36.818
I can't believe it!

04:36.901 --> 04:38.194
[Chota grunts]

04:38.278 --> 04:41.864
I was so worried
when you guys weren't back this morning.

04:41.948 --> 04:44.033
- It's so good to see you!
- [laughs]

04:44.117 --> 04:46.119
Hey, Chota.

04:46.202 --> 04:47.704
[grunts]
Easy.

04:47.787 --> 04:49.247
Are you hurt?

04:49.330 --> 04:51.249
[groans]
I'm okay.

04:54.043 --> 04:55.670
[Chota] Somebody radioed in?

04:56.212 --> 04:57.255
[Karube] Yeah.

04:59.090 --> 05:00.550
[Karube hissing in pain]

05:01.884 --> 05:02.802
Thanks.

05:04.512 --> 05:05.596
[groans]

05:06.139 --> 05:07.932
If we go to that Beach place,

05:08.641 --> 05:10.226
we might be able to find something.

05:10.727 --> 05:13.229
Like where everyone in the city
disappeared to?

05:13.938 --> 05:15.857
Maybe there's an evacuation shelter.

05:16.774 --> 05:18.401
Maybe everybody's there.

05:19.068 --> 05:23.114
The closest beaches to us are
in Shonan, Izu, and Ito, right?

05:24.449 --> 05:25.450
They're so far.

05:25.992 --> 05:28.911
But we can reach them in time.

05:30.872 --> 05:32.165
So, what do we think?

05:32.790 --> 05:34.000
Should we try going?

05:35.126 --> 05:36.044
My vote is…

05:37.545 --> 05:39.714
for now, we trust whoever this is.

05:41.049 --> 05:43.051
And how is Chota supposed to go?

05:44.927 --> 05:46.763
[exhales deeply]
That's a good point.

05:48.848 --> 05:50.141
And our visas…

05:51.934 --> 05:53.436
they expire today.

05:58.107 --> 05:59.984
Then we'll have to win the game today

06:00.651 --> 06:02.278
and extend your visas.

06:02.361 --> 06:03.529
Sound good?

06:04.530 --> 06:06.699
Then we'll go and look for
the Beach tomorrow.

06:23.925 --> 06:25.384
I'll go to the Beach.

06:27.178 --> 06:28.429
No matter what happens.

06:30.765 --> 06:32.183
I'll do whatever it takes.

06:36.938 --> 06:38.439
We have to believe there's hope.

06:42.568 --> 06:43.861
[exhales deeply]

06:43.945 --> 06:46.072
[calm music]

06:54.789 --> 06:57.583
[Usagi] It amazes me
that I'm willing to do anything

06:59.043 --> 07:00.920
in order to survive.

07:04.841 --> 07:07.385
If only we could choose to die
on our own terms.

07:22.817 --> 07:23.901
Arisu?

07:30.741 --> 07:31.993
What's the matter?

07:32.910 --> 07:35.329
[breathes deeply]

07:38.082 --> 07:39.792
- Nothing.
- [lighter clicks]

07:51.846 --> 07:53.014
[Shibuki] Say something.

07:55.808 --> 07:57.435
[Arisu] "Say something"? Like what?

07:58.227 --> 08:00.897
[Shibuki] Hm, let's see. Heard any gossip?

08:05.193 --> 08:07.820
- [Shibuki puffs]
- I saw someone die right in front of me.

08:10.656 --> 08:12.116
But I survived.

08:14.911 --> 08:16.245
So what should I say?

08:17.997 --> 08:19.123
That you were glad.

08:22.919 --> 08:24.420
Glad it wasn't you.

08:28.049 --> 08:30.009
I didn't think about that, but…

08:34.764 --> 08:35.765
Guess I was.

08:38.518 --> 08:40.436
All I thought about was surviving.

08:47.068 --> 08:49.195
Yeah, I get it. I'll tell you something.

08:52.448 --> 08:53.866
On my very first game day,

08:54.534 --> 08:56.077
everyone died except me.

09:00.706 --> 09:02.416
I didn't wanna die like them.

09:05.127 --> 09:06.212
What I wanted…

09:07.922 --> 09:09.715
What I wanted was to survive.

09:11.008 --> 09:13.010
[somber music]

09:20.518 --> 09:22.270
[Shibuki exhales]

09:28.401 --> 09:29.610
[Karube grunts]

09:33.573 --> 09:34.949
And… found it!

09:35.700 --> 09:36.867
[sighs]

09:38.369 --> 09:40.371
[somber music]

09:53.384 --> 09:55.052
Please be safe and all right.

10:09.150 --> 10:11.944
SHIBUYA STATION

10:13.112 --> 10:16.032
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

10:16.741 --> 10:17.950
[lights clunk]

10:22.121 --> 10:23.247
[sighs]

10:23.331 --> 10:24.540
He's late.

10:25.666 --> 10:27.376
Yeah, should we just go?

10:28.210 --> 10:30.004
No, we wait for Karube.

10:30.588 --> 10:33.132
If we don't join the game,
we could all die.

10:35.926 --> 10:37.094
[scoffs]

10:37.178 --> 10:38.262
Chota, let's go.

10:40.014 --> 10:41.974
They both have days left on their visa.

10:46.312 --> 10:47.480
[Chota grunts]

10:49.523 --> 10:51.609
[approaching footsteps]

10:51.692 --> 10:52.943
[gasps]

10:53.986 --> 10:54.987
[Arisu] Karube!

10:55.071 --> 10:56.989
[panting]

10:57.073 --> 10:58.115
Sorry.

10:58.199 --> 11:00.576
- I needed to get something.
- What do you mean, "sorry"?

11:05.581 --> 11:07.041
Shibuki and I…

11:07.708 --> 11:09.335
For us, there's no tomorrow.

11:12.046 --> 11:13.339
Why, what's going on?

11:14.715 --> 11:15.800
Don't be angry.

11:21.389 --> 11:23.140
We're wasting time. Let's go.

11:25.184 --> 11:26.227
Come on.

11:28.020 --> 11:29.021
Thank you.

11:31.565 --> 11:33.943
[ominous music]

11:59.218 --> 12:01.679
[ominous music continues]

12:30.875 --> 12:33.502
[exhales deeply]
Let's do this.

12:39.592 --> 12:41.510
[scanner beeping]

12:48.142 --> 12:52.062
SHINJUKU NATURAL BOTANICAL GARDEN

12:52.146 --> 12:54.398
[sinister music]

13:01.113 --> 13:04.033
[approaching footsteps]

13:20.799 --> 13:22.718
FEEL FREE TO USE ANY OF THESE

13:26.305 --> 13:28.724
FEEL FREE TO USE ANY OF THESE

13:28.807 --> 13:30.726
Are we gonna tear something apart?

13:32.478 --> 13:33.521
Huh…

13:38.567 --> 13:40.486
- This one.
- [Chota] Huh.

13:41.111 --> 13:43.030
Those look kinda cool.

13:46.951 --> 13:48.077
What the…

13:56.669 --> 13:58.671
[phone chimes]

13:58.754 --> 14:01.006
[phones ringing]

14:01.090 --> 14:03.342
FACE RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT FOR A MOMENT

14:04.510 --> 14:07.638
[chiming on PA]

14:07.721 --> 14:09.557
[announcer] Entries accepted.

14:11.308 --> 14:14.812
WELCOME! SPONSORED BY
SHINJUKU NATURAL BOTANICAL GARDEN

14:14.895 --> 14:19.233
[announcer] Put on the goggles
and proceed to the garden.

14:19.316 --> 14:21.569
[fanfare music playing]

14:25.656 --> 14:28.576
THIS WAY

14:28.659 --> 14:30.703
[fanfare music continues playing]

14:49.054 --> 14:51.515
- [clicks]
- [whirrs]

14:52.558 --> 14:53.475
[clicking]

14:53.559 --> 14:56.395
REGISTRATION IN PROGRESS
CURRENT PARTICIPANTS

14:56.478 --> 14:59.023
[scanner beeping]

15:01.442 --> 15:02.776
[Chota] What is this?

15:05.404 --> 15:08.240
[Arisu] My goggles recognized Chota
and the target cursor turned red.

15:08.324 --> 15:10.159
Yeah, when we look at each other.

15:10.242 --> 15:11.911
It must be a tracking function.

15:13.120 --> 15:14.705
What do they want us to do this time?

15:14.788 --> 15:15.831
[phones chiming]

15:15.915 --> 15:18.083
[announcer] Registration is now closed.

15:18.167 --> 15:19.752
The game will now commence.

15:20.336 --> 15:23.547
Difficulty, Seven of Hearts.

15:23.631 --> 15:24.965
Hearts.

15:25.549 --> 15:26.800
Hearts? Isn't that…

15:26.884 --> 15:28.302
[eerie music]

15:28.385 --> 15:30.429
[Nitobe] The suit of the playing cards
usually means

15:30.512 --> 15:32.097
what kind of game it's gonna be.

15:32.181 --> 15:35.100
Clubs is a team battle.
Diamonds is your wits.

15:35.184 --> 15:36.769
And as for Hearts…

15:37.353 --> 15:40.105
You play with people's hearts
and you tear them apart.

15:40.689 --> 15:42.858
Seven. Isn't that kinda difficult?

15:43.859 --> 15:45.653
[Shibuki] Hearts are the worst.

15:45.736 --> 15:46.779
[Chota] What do we do?

15:46.862 --> 15:48.113
[phones chiming]

15:48.697 --> 15:51.492
[announcer] Game, "Hide-and-seek".

15:51.575 --> 15:54.328
Rules. One person will be the wolf

15:54.411 --> 15:57.081
and the other three will be the lambs.

15:57.164 --> 16:01.210
A lamb found by the wolf
will become the next wolf

16:01.293 --> 16:04.338
and must hide so that
the wolf does not find them.

16:04.838 --> 16:06.173
Clear condition.

16:06.256 --> 16:09.718
Player who is the wolf at game's end
is the winner.

16:09.802 --> 16:11.929
Time limit, 15 minutes.

16:12.012 --> 16:13.973
When 15 minutes have passed,

16:14.473 --> 16:17.810
the collars fastened to the lambs' necks
will explode.

16:17.893 --> 16:19.019
What?

16:19.687 --> 16:20.980
[Chota] "Explode"?

16:21.480 --> 16:23.232
What does she mean?

16:25.025 --> 16:26.568
Do you know what this means?

16:27.653 --> 16:28.737
Know what?

16:29.530 --> 16:32.199
This means only one player will survive.

16:33.283 --> 16:34.368
What?

16:35.995 --> 16:37.204
We'll play hide-and-seek…

16:38.706 --> 16:40.958
Whoever's the wolf
at the end of the game wins.

16:41.583 --> 16:43.293
The other three will be dead.

16:44.712 --> 16:46.547
[shakily]
It's really very simple.

16:47.840 --> 16:48.799
[phones dings]

16:48.882 --> 16:51.635
[announcer] The first wolf is ID number

16:51.719 --> 16:57.558
1000247.

16:57.641 --> 16:59.476
Chota Segawa.

16:59.560 --> 17:01.812
[monitor boings, chimes]

17:02.771 --> 17:04.940
[breathing shakily]

17:06.233 --> 17:07.192
Really?

17:07.776 --> 17:09.486
[announcer] Game time limit.

17:09.570 --> 17:10.738
[beeping]

17:10.821 --> 17:13.574
[announcer] Fifteen minutes, commence.

17:14.324 --> 17:15.576
[timer dings]

17:17.369 --> 17:20.664
[breathing heavily]

17:24.251 --> 17:27.171
Stop it, Chota! If you try to take it off,
the collar might explode!

17:27.254 --> 17:29.298
- I don't care!
- [Arisu] Stop it!

17:29.381 --> 17:31.050
Leave me alone!

17:31.133 --> 17:32.384
[scanner beeps]

17:33.260 --> 17:35.220
[monitor boings, cheering]

17:37.347 --> 17:38.348
Arisu?

17:39.349 --> 17:41.018
[scanner beeps]

17:41.101 --> 17:43.020
[monitor boings, cheering]

17:47.608 --> 17:50.486
[Arisu] When we lock eyes,
the wolf role is passed on.

17:51.153 --> 17:52.780
That's the catch in this game.

17:54.031 --> 17:55.949
If the wolf doesn't survive,

17:56.033 --> 17:58.035
it's because the lambs killed it.

17:58.744 --> 18:00.537
What do we do, Arisu?

18:00.621 --> 18:02.039
[scanner beeps]

18:03.373 --> 18:04.500
It's bullshit!

18:04.583 --> 18:06.418
[scanner beeps]

18:06.502 --> 18:08.629
[monitor boings, cheering]

18:08.712 --> 18:10.714
[intense music]

18:11.882 --> 18:12.800
[Chota] Shibuki!

18:12.883 --> 18:15.385
The one that needs to hide
in this game is the wolf!

18:15.469 --> 18:18.305
- Are we going to die?
- [Karube] You will if you do nothing.

18:18.388 --> 18:19.556
But I'll be fine.

18:20.224 --> 18:21.183
Shibuki!

18:21.266 --> 18:22.101
[both] Karube!

18:22.810 --> 18:23.977
[Karube yelling]

18:25.145 --> 18:26.980
[panting]

18:31.026 --> 18:32.694
Stop running!

18:35.030 --> 18:36.115
[screams]

18:39.868 --> 18:41.078
[Karube] Shibuki!

18:41.161 --> 18:42.412
[hurried footsteps]

18:53.048 --> 18:55.968
TROPICAL RAINFOREST

18:56.885 --> 18:58.929
[panting]

19:04.518 --> 19:07.563
[approaching footsteps]

19:08.272 --> 19:10.274
[Karube panting]

19:14.653 --> 19:16.613
[breathing heavily]

19:23.579 --> 19:24.580
[Karube] Come out!

19:27.082 --> 19:28.333
Shibuki!

19:36.091 --> 19:37.384
[muffled pants]

19:40.971 --> 19:42.931
[grunting]

19:46.768 --> 19:48.020
Ah!

19:48.103 --> 19:49.813
[Chota shuddering]

19:53.025 --> 19:54.318
[whimpers]

19:56.987 --> 19:59.448
- [Chota] Can you read me, Shibuki?
- [panting]

20:00.616 --> 20:01.950
[Karube] Shibuki!

20:02.701 --> 20:03.785
[Chota] Stop running.

20:04.286 --> 20:06.788
Let's think of a way out of this together.

20:06.872 --> 20:08.749
[Shibuki whimpering]
I'm sorry.

20:09.416 --> 20:10.500
I'm sorry.

20:11.084 --> 20:12.836
- [screams]
- [thuds]

20:12.920 --> 20:14.630
[sobs, pants]

20:15.756 --> 20:18.842
There's no point apologizing now, huh?

20:18.926 --> 20:20.302
Huh?

20:20.385 --> 20:22.679
- Turn around!
- [Shibuki whimpering]

20:23.347 --> 20:24.723
[Chota] Stop it, Karube!

20:24.806 --> 20:26.600
[Karube] Come on, come on!

20:26.683 --> 20:28.435
[grunts]

20:29.144 --> 20:30.646
- [Karube] Turn around!
- [grunting]

20:32.189 --> 20:33.440
- [yells]
- [shrieks]

20:33.523 --> 20:34.733
[Shibuki grunts]

20:36.151 --> 20:37.486
[Karube grunts]

20:37.569 --> 20:38.987
[both grunting]

20:39.071 --> 20:41.406
[suspenseful music]

20:44.785 --> 20:46.453
[screams]

20:46.536 --> 20:48.789
[groans]

20:49.665 --> 20:51.124
[scanner beeping]

20:51.208 --> 20:53.293
- [monitor boings, cheering]
- [gasps]

20:55.379 --> 20:57.005
[Karube grunting]

20:57.089 --> 20:58.757
[Shibuki screams]

20:58.840 --> 21:03.345
- [grunting]
- [screaming in pain]

21:03.428 --> 21:06.056
- [sobbing]
- [Shibuki, Karube grunting]

21:07.224 --> 21:08.433
[sobbing continues]

21:09.309 --> 21:11.728
- [grunts]
- You fucking bitch!

21:11.812 --> 21:12.980
[Shibuki shrieks]

21:13.480 --> 21:15.607
[grunting]

21:17.025 --> 21:18.402
[Arisu] Karube!

21:18.485 --> 21:19.319
[gasps]

21:19.403 --> 21:20.946
- [scanner beeps]
- [gasps]

21:22.114 --> 21:24.032
[monitor boings, cheering]

21:24.116 --> 21:24.992
Arisu!

21:26.159 --> 21:28.328
Both of you, enough! Stop it!

21:28.412 --> 21:31.164
If we work together,
we might be able to figure this out!

21:31.248 --> 21:33.959
You're so naive, this is a Hearts game!

21:34.543 --> 21:35.669
[grunts]

21:37.045 --> 21:39.172
- [grunts]
- [groans in pain]

21:44.428 --> 21:46.430
[Chota] What's happening to us?

21:47.014 --> 21:50.100
[groans]

21:50.183 --> 21:51.601
[Chota] You're turning against each other!

21:51.685 --> 21:52.936
Damn you, Arisu!

21:53.645 --> 21:55.314
[Chota] We're friends, right?

21:58.400 --> 22:01.320
- [phone dings]
- [announcer] Ten minutes remaining.

22:01.403 --> 22:03.196
[sobs]

22:03.280 --> 22:04.406
[Karube growls]

22:04.948 --> 22:05.949
[Karube] Arisu!

22:06.033 --> 22:07.784
[shakingly]
O Holy Mother…

22:08.869 --> 22:10.078
Please forgive us

22:10.162 --> 22:12.205
- for our mortal sins.
- [Karube] Arisu!

22:13.498 --> 22:15.876
Our smiles are the light of hope.

22:16.960 --> 22:19.880
And you, Holy Mother, appear to us
when we smile.

22:20.589 --> 22:21.590
[Karube grunts]

22:21.673 --> 22:23.091
O Holy Mother…

22:24.468 --> 22:26.011
- Please forgive us…
- [Karube] Arisu!

22:26.094 --> 22:27.554
…for our mortal sins…

22:28.972 --> 22:31.600
Our smiles are the light of hope.

22:32.768 --> 22:36.146
And you, Holy Mother, appear to us
when we smile.

22:38.607 --> 22:41.276
[Chota sobbing]

22:42.527 --> 22:44.488
[Chota] O Holy Mother…

22:45.906 --> 22:48.283
Our smiles are the light of hope.

22:49.618 --> 22:52.245
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

22:52.996 --> 22:55.165
[tense music]

22:56.875 --> 22:58.085
[grunts]

22:59.836 --> 23:01.838
[Shibuki] Do you want to live or die?

23:02.422 --> 23:03.924
All I need is some time!

23:04.007 --> 23:06.802
I'll think of a way
to get out of this game!

23:06.885 --> 23:08.845
[Shibuki] You'll think of a way out, huh?

23:11.681 --> 23:13.975
You just want to be the only survivor.

23:16.144 --> 23:18.480
It doesn't matter to you if you're dead.

23:20.273 --> 23:21.525
Make me the wolf.

23:22.150 --> 23:24.027
Your life is shit anyway!

23:24.111 --> 23:25.570
[panting]

23:25.654 --> 23:30.075
Where's the justice when someone
who has the desire to live dies?

23:31.993 --> 23:33.078
[Karube] Arisu.

23:34.996 --> 23:37.624
We can't all survive in this game!

23:38.416 --> 23:40.710
[breathing heavily]

23:42.170 --> 23:44.172
- [Shibuki yells]
- [Chota screams]

23:44.256 --> 23:45.173
[both grunt]

23:46.925 --> 23:48.426
- [grunts]
- [Arisu yelps]

23:48.510 --> 23:49.678
Chota!

23:49.761 --> 23:52.514
- [Shibuki] Let me go!
- Go! Run!

23:54.808 --> 23:55.684
[Shibuki] Let me go!

23:57.144 --> 23:58.353
[Shibuki] Stop!

23:59.271 --> 24:01.815
[suspenseful music]

24:03.608 --> 24:05.735
- [both grunting]
- Let me go!

24:05.819 --> 24:08.697
I took care of you!

24:09.281 --> 24:11.741
You don't know
what your friends really are!

24:12.367 --> 24:13.702
[Shibuki] Let me go!

24:15.203 --> 24:16.037
Let me go!

24:16.121 --> 24:18.748
- [Chota] O Holy Mother…
- [Shibuki] Let me go!

24:18.832 --> 24:20.876
[suspenseful music]

24:22.627 --> 24:24.796
[announcer] Eight minutes remaining.

24:27.132 --> 24:28.842
[Shibuki] Let go!

24:28.925 --> 24:31.178
[clattering]

24:33.597 --> 24:35.807
[Shibuki screaming]

24:38.185 --> 24:39.936
[Karube] Arisu!

24:42.272 --> 24:43.899
[pants]

24:44.608 --> 24:46.568
Where are you, Arisu? Come out!

24:46.651 --> 24:47.777
[growls]

24:47.861 --> 24:49.321
[Arisu] Come on, damn it.

24:50.447 --> 24:53.033
[Karube] You're just gonna hide
until time runs out?

24:53.116 --> 24:54.534
[Arisu] Ugh, shit!

24:55.035 --> 24:57.120
[Karube panting]

24:57.204 --> 24:59.331
[Karube] Come on, Arisu.

24:59.414 --> 25:01.333
- You were playing us all.
- [Arisu grunts]

25:02.876 --> 25:05.795
[Karube] And you said
it'll work out if we cooperate.

25:08.048 --> 25:11.509
From the very start of this,
you wanted to be the only survivor!

25:11.593 --> 25:13.929
[pants, groans]

25:15.222 --> 25:17.140
[grunting]

25:19.434 --> 25:20.393
[screams]

25:26.107 --> 25:28.276
[suspenseful music]

25:30.695 --> 25:31.821
[grunts]

25:40.247 --> 25:42.082
- [timer trilling]
- [explodes]

25:42.165 --> 25:44.251
[ominous music]

25:49.005 --> 25:52.801
- [clattering]
- [sobs]

25:53.510 --> 25:56.513
- [whimpers]
- [Chota yells]

25:59.975 --> 26:00.934
[Shibuki yelps]

26:01.559 --> 26:04.020
I don't know what to do.

26:04.104 --> 26:06.648
- [Shibuki] Get off of me!
- [Chota grunting]

26:06.731 --> 26:07.649
I'm sorry.

26:08.900 --> 26:09.985
I'm sorry!

26:11.778 --> 26:14.572
[Karube] Ha!
What's the use of saying sorry?

26:14.656 --> 26:16.116
Arisu!

26:17.534 --> 26:18.660
[grunts]

26:19.411 --> 26:21.204
In the end, that's…

26:21.288 --> 26:22.372
all you ever do.

26:23.665 --> 26:24.874
[groans]

26:27.794 --> 26:30.130
[Karube] Ever since
you dropped out of school…

26:30.213 --> 26:31.214
[Karube grunts]

26:33.049 --> 26:35.802
[Karube] All you do is say sorry!

26:35.885 --> 26:37.887
- [Karube] Arisu!
- I'm sorry.

26:38.513 --> 26:39.597
[sobbing]
I'm sorry!

26:40.765 --> 26:41.891
I'm sorry.

26:50.233 --> 26:52.360
[Kenji] Congratulations
on your acceptance, Hajime.

26:52.444 --> 26:54.779
You really accomplished something.

26:54.863 --> 26:56.948
I know your mother would be happy too.

26:57.032 --> 26:59.576
And this is just the beginning.

27:01.202 --> 27:03.705
I'll see it through.
I don't want to end up like Ryohei.

27:04.331 --> 27:08.084
I can't teach Ryohei anything,
but you're different.

27:08.168 --> 27:09.878
Inside you, there's ambition.

27:10.879 --> 27:13.131
You're very different from your brother.

27:15.800 --> 27:18.553
Ryohei, why don't you come over
and join us?

27:21.389 --> 27:23.725
[whirring on phone]

27:30.774 --> 27:34.027
[Karube panting]
If you're happy being a loser…

27:34.110 --> 27:35.278
[Karube pants]

27:35.362 --> 27:38.239
[Karube] …then let me be the wolf!

27:38.323 --> 27:40.325
[sobs]

27:42.952 --> 27:44.621
[Karube] Arisu!

27:46.790 --> 27:48.083
[Karube groans]

27:49.626 --> 27:51.169
- [grunts]
- [ring clatters]

27:51.920 --> 27:53.296
[groans]

27:53.380 --> 27:56.299
- [phone dings]
- [announcer] Five minutes remaining.

27:56.383 --> 27:57.675
[sobbing]

27:58.510 --> 28:00.011
[Chota] I've had enough.

28:00.095 --> 28:01.805
[Shibuki whimpering]

28:01.888 --> 28:06.434
I don't care who survives in the end.

28:11.481 --> 28:12.482
But…

28:14.359 --> 28:17.654
But I don't want it to end this way.

28:17.737 --> 28:19.823
- [Shibuki grunting]
- [sobs, grunts]

28:19.906 --> 28:22.158
[somber music]

28:26.996 --> 28:28.289
[grunts]

28:40.009 --> 28:42.679
[Emi] Is this about Arisu and Chota again?

28:42.762 --> 28:44.764
[somber music]

28:48.643 --> 28:52.021
[soft chuckle]
You know, you really are very kind.

28:56.401 --> 28:58.153
[laughs]

29:07.954 --> 29:10.206
[somber music continues]

29:20.175 --> 29:21.468
[sniffles]

29:22.927 --> 29:25.138
[Arisu sobs]

29:37.692 --> 29:39.277
[Kenji] I don't expect anything from you

29:39.360 --> 29:41.529
and you never fail to disappoint me
in that regard.

29:43.198 --> 29:44.324
So, did you…

29:55.168 --> 29:57.295
[somber music continues]

30:10.725 --> 30:12.894
[somber music builds]

30:18.024 --> 30:20.109
[Chota, Arisu, Karube laughing]

30:28.409 --> 30:30.787
[indistinct chatter]

30:32.747 --> 30:34.332
This noodle is so good!

30:37.001 --> 30:38.670
[laughs]

30:39.420 --> 30:41.130
You look like you can't eat noodles…

30:43.383 --> 30:45.176
[all laughing, cheering]

30:45.260 --> 30:46.344
[Chota] Come on, man!

30:47.220 --> 30:49.097
[Arisu] Come on, Karube, faster!

30:51.641 --> 30:53.935
[soft chorale music]

31:00.817 --> 31:04.237
[sobbing]

31:10.952 --> 31:12.120
[Karube] Guys.

31:14.831 --> 31:17.709
I got this… dream.

31:18.543 --> 31:22.213
I wanna buy a huge farm in Australia.

31:23.381 --> 31:28.469
Then I'll invite you guys over,
and we'll drink beer in the morning.

31:28.553 --> 31:30.179
[laughs]
[Chota] That sounds nice!

31:30.263 --> 31:32.724
And I'll deliver
triple grade-A steaks to you

31:32.807 --> 31:35.476
with my drone delivery service.

31:35.560 --> 31:38.521
My drones will be fully automated,
I'll develop an app for them!

31:38.605 --> 31:40.273
[laughs]

31:40.356 --> 31:43.568
[Karube] All right then.
Cheers to our future.

31:43.651 --> 31:44.819
[Chota] Cheers!

31:44.903 --> 31:46.905
[Karube] You better keep your promise,
you hear?

31:46.988 --> 31:48.615
[Karube chuckles]

31:48.698 --> 31:50.825
[sobs]

31:56.915 --> 31:59.083
[soft chorale music continues]

32:03.087 --> 32:04.255
[sniffles]

32:12.931 --> 32:15.016
[soft chorale music continues]

32:29.322 --> 32:31.699
- [groans]
- [Shibuki pants]

32:32.283 --> 32:35.203
[sobbing]

32:36.454 --> 32:37.664
[phone chimes]

32:38.706 --> 32:40.875
[announcer] Three minutes remaining.

32:53.388 --> 32:56.099
Guys, I'll… quit.

32:59.018 --> 33:02.647
[Arisu] I'll… drop out of this game.

33:06.234 --> 33:07.819
[sniffs]
You're all…

33:09.237 --> 33:11.239
You're all that matters to me.

33:14.117 --> 33:16.452
If someone has to lose at this game…

33:18.037 --> 33:19.956
- [sniffs]
- …let it be me.

33:23.918 --> 33:25.253
I'm leaving the game.

33:28.464 --> 33:32.010
Karube? Chota? Karube.

33:33.511 --> 33:35.638
[somber music]

33:35.722 --> 33:37.515
[Arisu] Karube, Chota?

33:45.064 --> 33:46.190
[Arisu] Karube!

33:46.899 --> 33:48.192
Chota!

33:49.110 --> 33:52.321
- [Arisu] Guys!
- [hurried footsteps]

33:55.783 --> 33:56.868
Chota!

33:59.162 --> 33:59.996
Chota!

34:01.497 --> 34:03.041
Where are you?

34:03.124 --> 34:04.167
Chota!

34:04.250 --> 34:06.711
[muffled yelling]

34:08.171 --> 34:10.715
[leaves rustling]

34:11.758 --> 34:13.968
Chota!
[panting]

34:16.763 --> 34:17.889
Chota?

34:19.807 --> 34:20.850
Where are you?

34:20.933 --> 34:23.519
- [Arisu] Chota!
- [Shibuki muffled groans]

34:23.603 --> 34:26.522
YOU BECOME THE WOLF IF YOU ARE FOUND.
HIDE SO THAT THE WOLF WON'T FIND YOU.

34:27.106 --> 34:28.191
Karube!

34:29.358 --> 34:30.568
Chota!

34:31.277 --> 34:32.528
[pants]

34:33.279 --> 34:34.989
Come out! Let's talk!

34:36.282 --> 34:37.408
Guys!

34:38.159 --> 34:41.079
HIDE SO THAT THE WOLF WON'T FIND YOU

34:42.288 --> 34:45.583
[approaching footsteps]

34:46.667 --> 34:49.337
[Arisu] Karube! Where are you?

34:51.631 --> 34:53.674
Why won't you guys answer me?

34:56.552 --> 34:58.054
Karube!

35:02.183 --> 35:06.104
HIDE WELL, LAMB

35:06.187 --> 35:08.481
[Arisu pants]
Where are you guys?

35:09.899 --> 35:11.025
Karube!

35:13.945 --> 35:15.238
[Arisu] Chota!

35:18.199 --> 35:19.492
Chota!

35:21.494 --> 35:23.037
Karube!

35:23.121 --> 35:25.206
[Arisu] Come out, please!

35:25.957 --> 35:27.875
[grunts]
Stop yelling.

35:30.086 --> 35:31.212
Karube!

35:36.008 --> 35:38.511
- [clatters]
- [exhales deeply]

35:40.346 --> 35:42.348
Always laughing like idiots,

35:43.599 --> 35:45.268
drinking the night away…

35:47.728 --> 35:49.313
When I'm with you guys,

35:50.148 --> 35:52.233
I forget about all my problems.

35:54.026 --> 35:55.820
[Karube] Hey, do you guys remember?

35:55.903 --> 35:59.699
That fricking hot day
when we made noodles with shaved ice?

35:59.782 --> 36:02.451
Karube, where are you?

36:04.579 --> 36:05.872
Karube!

36:05.955 --> 36:07.999
[somber music]

36:09.750 --> 36:12.295
We laughed a lot that day, didn't we?

36:12.378 --> 36:14.422
[laughs]

36:15.631 --> 36:16.924
Chota?

36:17.008 --> 36:20.052
Chota laughed so hard
that noodles came out from his nose.

36:20.136 --> 36:21.012
[laughs]

36:21.971 --> 36:24.891
I thought we said
we'd keep that our secret.

36:24.974 --> 36:26.934
Where are you, Chota?

36:27.602 --> 36:28.811
Karube!

36:30.229 --> 36:31.480
Arisu.

36:33.441 --> 36:34.775
Live for us.

36:35.276 --> 36:37.278
[somber music continues]

36:45.369 --> 36:46.996
[Arisu] Karube!

36:47.079 --> 36:48.539
- [phone dings]
- [Arisu] Chota!

36:48.623 --> 36:51.000
[announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.

36:56.797 --> 36:58.591
[sobs]

37:02.887 --> 37:03.846
[Arisu] It can't be me!

37:04.597 --> 37:06.557
I shouldn't be the one to live!

37:07.767 --> 37:09.060
[announcer] Twenty seconds.

37:09.143 --> 37:10.311
[Karube] I'm behind you.

37:11.854 --> 37:12.688
[puffs]

37:13.314 --> 37:14.357
[whimpers]

37:14.941 --> 37:16.192
[Chota] I'm sorry.

37:16.943 --> 37:19.278
I'm sorry, Shibuki.

37:19.362 --> 37:22.031
- [announcer] Ten seconds.
- Arisu.

37:24.450 --> 37:25.368
Thank you.

37:25.451 --> 37:29.038
- [announcer] Five, four, three, two…
- Karube!

37:29.121 --> 37:30.957
- [announcer] …one.
- [Arisu] Karube!

37:31.040 --> 37:32.458
[explodes]

37:32.541 --> 37:34.418
[sobbing]

37:37.213 --> 37:38.506
[thuds]

38:00.903 --> 38:02.780
[cries]

38:16.168 --> 38:17.253
[wails]

38:23.050 --> 38:25.052
[screaming]

38:39.734 --> 38:41.861
[Arisu screaming continues]

38:41.944 --> 38:44.363
[tragic music]

39:01.255 --> 39:03.257
[inaudible screaming]

39:04.216 --> 39:06.510
[shouts]

39:19.065 --> 39:21.275
[ominous music]

39:22.360 --> 39:24.362
[wailing]

39:27.198 --> 39:28.491
[scream echos]

39:32.244 --> 39:34.663
[closing theme music]
